        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>
  We are open about the last row: loop impedance and RCD testing need a dedicated multifunction installation tester, and that is not something CIE supplies. For the rest of the sequence, CIE covers <a href={u('/products/digital-insulation-testers/')}>digital insulation testers</a> with selectable test voltages, <a href={u('/products/earth-tester/')}>earth resistance testers</a>, <a href={u('/products/multimeters/')}>multimeters</a> and <a href={u('/products/phase-sequence-indicators/')}>phase sequence indicators</a>.
</p>

<h2 id="records">Record Everything</h2>

<p>
  A verification is only as good as its paperwork. Record the instrument serial number, the test voltage actually applied, the reading for each circuit and the date. Clients and inspectors in every market will ask for it, and a calibrated instrument with a traceable record protects the contractor if a result is ever questioned. For how often to recalibrate, read our <a href={u('/blog/calibration-interval-guide/')}>calibration interval guide</a>.
</p>

